WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
On the western side of the Atlantic, the
Gulf Stream carries warm tropical water

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.270
towards the pole.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.510
Its extension, the North Atlantic Drift,
carries that warm water on towards north-west

4
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.090
Europe.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.350
NOAA calls the Gulf Stream the main
conveyor of heat from south to north in the

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.470
Atlantic.

7
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.890
So is the Gulf Stream the reason
north-west Europe's winters are mild?

8
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll trace
the gyres at the surface,

9
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.530
and the global conveyor belt that
loops deep beneath the oceans.

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.610
Then you'll weigh an
influential model study,

11
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.950
and ask how the Atlantic
conveyor may change this century.

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.370
Your mission: decide whether the Gulf
Stream explains north-west Europe's mild

13
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.190
winters.
